A||||2||SCCA FIERO||Oil Pressure gauge... or sender?||||1||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||09-05-2000||10:37 PM||||My oil pressure gauge reads almost as high as the guauge will go. It does this when I turn the key to run, then to start, and while the car is at idle or 5k rpm's. Is it the gauge or the sender?<P>I'm trying to get everything on my car working...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||09-05-2000||11:21 PM||||99% of the time it's the sender.. There's a "breather vent" on top of it that just let's water get in there and short it out.  If/when you get a new one fill the vent hole with silicone or rtv or something.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blaster||09-06-2000||12:00 AM||||Hey... I'll tell ya what I did to check mine.  Before I rebuilt my engine, I was getting CRAPPY oil pressure.  So to check to see if it was the gauge or the sender, I went to the autoparts store and bought a cheap mechanical oil pressure gauge.  Hooked it up and let the car warm up.  Wasn't really happy with the results obviously since I had to rebuild.  But doing this is cheaper than just going and buying a oil pressure sensor. ($30) Hope it helps. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
